  Pauli strings generated from the JW structure; coefficients are irrelevant
  to both the term count and the qubit-wise-commuting grouping.

     N   T terms  G groups     T/G    T/N^4    G/N^3
  --------------------------------------------------
     6       171        75    2.28    0.132    0.347
     8       652       259    2.52    0.159    0.506
    10      1825       656    2.78    0.182    0.656
    12      4170      1420    2.94    0.201    0.822

  fitted exponents:   T ~ N^4.61    G ~ N^4.24    T/G ~ N^0.37
  claimed:            T ~ N^4.00    G ~ N^3.00    T/G ~ N^1.00

============================================================================================
WHAT THAT DOES TO THE V3 / V4 CHOICE, using MEASURED G
============================================================================================
  V3: 3 circuits/epoch, depth ~ Sigma_a r_a * T * 16 gates (kappa=3 -> Sigma=4)
  V4: (G+2) circuits/epoch, depth ~ ansatz

     N        T       G   V3 depth    V3 dur  V3 $/epoch  V4 $/epoch   winner
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
     6      171      75      10944      766us        20.0       126.9       V3
     8      652     259      41728     2921us        62.3       430.4       V3
    10     1825     656     116800     8176us       165.7      1085.6       V3
    12     4170    1420     266880    18682us       372.2      2347.4       V3

  The crossover here is the whole chemistry case. If V3 loses at every N
  the THC build is what rescues it - depth Theta(T) -> Theta(N^2) - and if
  V3 already wins, the build is unnecessary and the priority is wrong.
